usage: openscrub-web [-h] [--port PORT] [--host HOST] [--token TOKEN] [--http]
                     [--retain-days RETAIN_DAYS]
                     [--max-upload-gb MAX_UPLOAD_GB]

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --port PORT
  --host HOST
  --token TOKEN         require this access token on every request (default:
                        open — anyone on the network can use the server)
  --http                serve plain HTTP (not recommended: video uploads and
                        previews contain PII and would cross the network
                        unencrypted)
  --retain-days RETAIN_DAYS
                        auto-delete job folders (which contain PII) after this
                        many days (default 7; 0 = keep forever)
  --max-upload-gb MAX_UPLOAD_GB
                        largest browser upload accepted, in GB (default 8; 0 =
                        unlimited; env OPENSCRUB_MAX_UPLOAD_GB works too).
                        Very large files are better served in place via the
                        'path on the server' box than uploaded.
